RDS PostgreSQL
└── elis_ms_pdfi
    │
    ├── Database owner
    │   └── elis_ms_pdfi
    │
    ├── elis_ms_pfvs
    │   ├── Schema owner/login: elis_ms_pfvs
    │   │      └── Dev deployment / DDL
    │   │
    │   ├── IAM owner: elis_ms_pfvs_iam
    │   │      └── Alternate IAM deployment access
    │   │
    │   ├── App user: elis_ms_pfvs_app
    │   │
    │   ├── App IAM: elis_ms_pfvs_app_iam
    │   │
    │   ├── Read role
    │   └── Write role
    │
    ├── elis_ms_epis
    ├── elis_ms_pdfi_ss
    ├── elis_ms_pdfi_ps
    └── elis_ms_pdfi_lgs
Moving away from following ELIS out-of-date standards:
(1) removed custom tablespace.  (AWS RDS PostgreSQL, tablespaces generally do not give you separate physical disks, separate storage performance, or separate backup behavior the way they might in a self-managed PostgreSQL environment. RDS manages the underlying storage for you.)
(2) _app user gets _write_role instead of schema owner role.  (prevent it from deploying schema changes)
